# The issue: L_INTHASBITS(SIZE_Bx) = L_INTHASBITS(17)
# L_INTHASBITS(b) checks if UINT_MAX >> (b-1) >= 1
# UINT_MAX = 2^32-1
# UINT_MAX >> 16 = 2^16-1 >= 1 -> TRUE
# So we SHOULD use ((1<<SIZE_Bx)-1)!
# 
# But L_INTHASBITS is checking if 'int' has at least b bits.
# L_INTHASBITS(b) = ((UINT_MAX >> ((b) - 1)) >= 1)
# For b=17: UINT_MAX >> 16 = 0xFFFF >= 1 = TRUE
# So we use (1<<SIZE_Bx)-1 = (1<<17)-1 = 131071
# OFFSET_sBx = 131071 >> 1 = 65535
# 
# So OFFSET_sBx SHOULD be 65535!
# 
# Let me verify what the test shows:
# LOADI sBx = -65535 means the raw Bx value is 0
# But we should have created Bx = 1 + 65535 = 65536
# 
